+# Sources consulted
+
+These pages were fetched over the live network before the design was implemented.
+
+| Published source | URL | Access date | Compatibility or path decision supported |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Broadcom KB 414400, *How to upgrade/converge from VMware Live Site Recovery to VMware Live Recovery Appliance* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/414400/how-to-upgradeconverge-from-vmware-live.html | 2026-08-14 | VMware Live Site Recovery and vSphere Replication at 9.0.2.2 converge rather than directly upgrade to the combined VMware Live Recovery 9.0.4 appliance; 9.0.4 supports vSphere/ESX 8.0 U3 and later. |
+| Broadcom KB 440630, *Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html | 2026-08-14 | An estate with vCenter/ESX 8.x and NSX 4.x must use VCF Installer converge plus convert/import rather than independent component upgrade routes. The pinned component steps are stages inside that workflow. |
+| Broadcom KB 410435, *Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html | 2026-08-14 | VCF 9.x aligns vCenter, ESX, vSAN, NSX, and recovery components on the unified release convention, including the 9.0.2.0 bridge and 9.1.0.0 target lines. |
+| Broadcom KB 313905, *Build numbers and versions of VMware Live Site Recovery / VMware Site Recovery Manager* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/313905 | 2026-08-14 | Confirms the inventoried Live Site Recovery 9.0.2.2 line, the later standalone 9.0.2.4 boundary, and the combined VMware Live Recovery 9.0.4 successor line. |
+| Broadcom KB 319887, *Build numbers and versions of VMware vSphere Replication Appliance* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/319887/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-vsp.html | 2026-08-14 | Confirms vSphere Replication 9.0.2.2, the standalone 9.0.2.3 boundary, and inclusion in the combined VMware Live Recovery 9.0.4 successor. |
+| Broadcom KB 426655, *Build numbers and versions of VCF Protection and Recovery* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/426655/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-liv.html | 2026-08-14 | VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1 is the renamed, VCF-integrated successor to the VMware Live Recovery 9.0.x line. |
+| Broadcom KB 390634, *Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html | 2026-08-14 | Core lifecycle ordering is NSX, vCenter, then ESXi; vSAN finalization follows the ESX host lifecycle boundary. |
+| Broadcom KB 326316, *VMware vCenter Server versions and build numbers* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326316/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-vce.html | 2026-08-14 | Confirms the inventoried vCenter 8.0.3.00700 release and the 9.0.2.0 bridge and 9.1 target release lines selected by the pinned path. |
+| Broadcom KB 316595, *Build numbers and versions of VMware ESXi/ESX* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/316595 | 2026-08-14 | Confirms ESXi 8.0.3 P07, ESX 9.0.2.0, and ESX 9.1 release identities used in the host path. |
+| Broadcom KB 326465, *Build numbers and versions of VMware vSAN* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?articleNumber=326465 | 2026-08-14 | vSAN is bound to the ESXi/ESX release, supporting the plan's upgrade-with-ESX disposition from vSAN 8.0 U3 through the pinned 9.0.2.0 and 9.1.0.0 stages. |
+| Broadcom KB 317797, *Build numbers and versions of VMware NSX/NSX-T Data Center* | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317797/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-nsx.html | 2026-08-14 | Confirms the NSX 4.2.3.3 source and unified 9.0.2.0 and 9.1.0.0 release lines selected by the pinned path. |
+| `vmware/vcf-api-specs`, tag `9.1.0.0`, VCF Installer OpenAPI document | https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json | 2026-08-14 | Supplies the authoritative `SddcSpec` structure used for the target management domain. |
